# Project Rules

Project rules are organized by skill area in `.cursor/rules/` directory:

## Core Development Skills
- **Architecture & Design**: `.cursor/rules/architecture-design.mdc` - SOLID principles, design patterns, modularity
- **Code Quality**: `.cursor/rules/code-quality.mdc` - Clean code, maintainability, DRY, KISS, YAGNI
- **TypeScript**: `.cursor/rules/typescript.mdc` - TypeScript standards and best practices
- **React & Next.js**: `.cursor/rules/react-nextjs.mdc` - React 19 and Next.js 16 standards
- **UI & Styling**: `.cursor/rules/ui-styling.mdc` - Shadcn UI, Radix UI, Tailwind 4 guidelines

## Specialized Skills
- **Testing**: `.cursor/rules/testing.mdc` - Testing standards and guidelines (Jest, Testing Library)
- **API Design**: `.cursor/rules/api-design.mdc` - RESTful API design principles
- **Security**: `.cursor/rules/security.mdc` - Security best practices
- **Error Handling**: `.cursor/rules/error-handling.mdc` - Error handling patterns
- **Performance**: `.cursor/rules/performance.mdc` - Performance optimization strategies
- **Accessibility**: `.cursor/rules/accessibility.mdc` - WCAG accessibility standards

## Process & Workflow
- **Process & Workflow**: `.cursor/rules/process-workflow.mdc` - Git, code reviews, documentation, CI/CD

All rules are automatically applied by Cursor based on their metadata (alwaysApply, globs, etc.).

